# Citation metadata for the Relaxed Memory Model Zoo dataset.
#
# Generated from CITATION.cff.in by tools/render.py: the version and release date
# below are stamped in from the git tag at build time (see RELEASING.md), and the
# result is published with the dataset it describes, at
#
#   https://rmm-zoo.kissig.org/data/CITATION.cff
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Relaxed Memory Model Zoo (the dataset or the map), please cite it as below."
title: "The Relaxed Memory Model Zoo"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, openly published map of hardware and programming-language
  memory models, ordered by the inclusion of their allowed execution
  behaviours (strength), together with the machine-readable dataset
  (models.json: models, ordering edges with typed evidence, references, and
  per-model property vectors) behind it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kissig
    given-names: Christian
version: "@VERSION@"
date-released: "@DATE@"
license: BSD-3-Clause
url: "https://rmm-zoo.kissig.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/christiankissig/rmm-zoo-dataset"
keywords:
  - weak memory models
  - relaxed memory
  - memory consistency
  - shared-memory concurrency
  - litmus tests
